WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.993
Customer Care and Complaints.

2
00:00:02.273 --> 00:00:06.646
Day 52 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.396 --> 00:00:09.420
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:20.409
Today's goal: call or chat with customer care for mobile, internet, apps and services, explain the issue fast, stay calm, escalate politely, and get a complaint number.

5
00:00:21.759 --> 00:00:22.613
Part 1.

6
00:00:22.893 --> 00:00:23.853
Key words.

7
00:00:25.103 --> 00:00:26.447
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:26.727 --> 00:00:47.313
Word or phrase, and Meaning. customer care or support or helpline: the service team. complaint or ticket or reference number: the record of your issue. escalate or supervisor or nodal officer: take it to a higher level. recharge or plan or postpaid or prepaid: mobile plans. network issue or no

9
00:00:47.593 --> 00:00:58.025
signal or slow speed or outage: connection problems. technician visit: someone comes to your home. refund or reversal or chargeback: money back.

10
00:00:58.305 --> 00:01:01.207
TAT (turnaround time): how long they'll take.

11
00:01:02.557 --> 00:01:03.431
Part 2.

12
00:01:03.711 --> 00:01:05.013
The complaint formula.

13
00:01:06.263 --> 00:01:07.201
You could say:

14
00:01:07.481 --> 00:01:15.375
Hi, my name is Ashish Gupta, and my account number is 7781 2345.

15
00:01:15.655 --> 00:01:19.175
My home internet hasn't been working since yesterday evening.

16
00:01:19.455 --> 00:01:21.033
The router shows a red light.

17
00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:22.807
I've restarted it twice.

18
00:01:23.087 --> 00:01:25.412
I'd like a technician visit today, please.

19
00:01:26.762 --> 00:01:27.658
Part 3.

20
00:01:27.938 --> 00:01:29.154
Questions you'll ask.

21
00:01:30.404 --> 00:01:32.345
Could I have the complaint number, please?

22
00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.889
How long will it take to fix? / What's the TAT?

23
00:01:36.169 --> 00:01:39.071
Will I get a credit for the days the service didn't work?

24
00:01:39.351 --> 00:01:43.148
Could you escalate this, please? / Could I speak to your supervisor?

25
00:01:43.428 --> 00:01:46.393
Can you send me the details by email or SMS?

26
00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:50.513
Why was I charged 499 rupeesextra this month?

27
00:01:51.863 --> 00:01:52.781
Part 4.

28
00:01:53.061 --> 00:01:55.258
Conversation 1: internet down.

29
00:01:56.508 --> 00:01:58.535
Here is how the conversation goes.

30
00:01:58.815 --> 00:02:00.713
Thank you for calling FastNet.

31
00:02:00.993 --> 00:02:02.465
My name is Rohit.

32
00:02:02.745 --> 00:02:04.068
How may I help you?

33
00:02:04.348 --> 00:02:05.457
Hi Rohit.

34
00:02:05.737 --> 00:02:09.279
My home internet has been down since 8 pm yesterday.

35
00:02:09.559 --> 00:02:12.225
The account is in the name of Ashish Gupta.

36
00:02:12.505 --> 00:02:14.639
May I have your registered mobile number?

37
00:02:14.919 --> 00:02:20.188
It's 98450 12345.

38
00:02:21.538 --> 00:02:23.138
The conversation continues.

39
00:02:23.418 --> 00:02:24.527
Thank you.

40
00:02:24.807 --> 00:02:26.706
Have you tried restarting the router?

41
00:02:26.986 --> 00:02:28.095
Yes, twice.

42
00:02:28.375 --> 00:02:30.210
The internet light is red.

43
00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.325
I can see an outage in your area.

44
00:02:32.605 --> 00:02:34.439
It should be fixed in four hours.

45
00:02:34.719 --> 00:02:37.301
I work from home, so this is urgent.

46
00:02:37.581 --> 00:02:39.437
Could you give me a complaint number?

47
00:02:39.717 --> 00:02:43.386
Sure, it's FN-552190.

48
00:02:44.736 --> 00:02:46.336
The conversation continues.

49
00:02:46.616 --> 00:02:47.555
Thank you.

50
00:02:47.835 --> 00:02:50.053
Will I get a credit for the downtime?

51
00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:53.384
Yes, the credit will be added automatically to your next bill.

52
00:02:53.664 --> 00:02:54.411
Great.

53
00:02:54.691 --> 00:02:58.765
If it isn't fixed by 2 pm, I'll call back with this number.

54
00:03:00.115 --> 00:03:01.075
Part 5.

55
00:03:01.355 --> 00:03:04.257
Conversation 2: escalating a wrong charge.

56
00:03:05.507 --> 00:03:07.533
Here is how the conversation goes.

57
00:03:07.813 --> 00:03:15.173
Hi, I called twice about a wrong charge of 1,200 rupeeson my bill, but it hasn't been fixed.

58
00:03:15.453 --> 00:03:16.520
I'm sorry.

59
00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.507
Could you share the complaint number?

60
00:03:18.787 --> 00:03:22.093
It's MB-81234.

61
00:03:22.373 --> 00:03:26.981
I was charged for international roaming, but I haven't travelled abroad.

62
00:03:27.261 --> 00:03:28.776
I can see the complaint.

63
00:03:29.056 --> 00:03:30.485
It's still under review.

64
00:03:31.835 --> 00:03:33.435
The conversation continues.

65
00:03:33.715 --> 00:03:35.273
It's been ten days.

66
00:03:35.553 --> 00:03:37.686
I'd like this escalated, please.

67
00:03:37.966 --> 00:03:40.035
Could I speak to a supervisor?

68
00:03:40.315 --> 00:03:42.107
Please hold, I'll transfer you.

69
00:03:42.387 --> 00:03:44.606
Hello, I'm Anjali, the supervisor.

70
00:03:44.886 --> 00:03:47.147
I've checked: the charge was a system error.

71
00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:48.366
Thank you.

72
00:03:48.646 --> 00:03:50.673
When will the amount be reversed?

73
00:03:52.023 --> 00:03:53.623
The conversation continues.

74
00:03:53.903 --> 00:03:55.545
Within 48 hours.

75
00:03:55.825 --> 00:03:57.916
You'll get an SMS confirmation.

76
00:03:58.196 --> 00:04:00.756
Could you also confirm it by email, please?

77
00:04:01.036 --> 00:04:02.487
Yes, I'll send it now.

78
00:04:03.837 --> 00:04:04.775
Part 6.

79
00:04:05.055 --> 00:04:06.826
Staying calm (and effective).

80
00:04:08.076 --> 00:04:09.420
Here is a quick table:

81
00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:10.831
Avoid, and Try.

82
00:04:11.111 --> 00:04:12.412
Shouting at the agent:

83
00:04:12.692 --> 00:04:14.185
I know it's not your fault.

84
00:04:14.465 --> 00:04:16.108
I just need this fixed today.

85
00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:18.137
Explaining the whole story again:

86
00:04:18.417 --> 00:04:21.233
Here's my complaint number, and here's what's still pending.

87
00:04:21.513 --> 00:04:23.305
Ending the call without a number:

88
00:04:23.585 --> 00:04:26.167
Before we finish, could I have the reference number?

89
00:04:27.517 --> 00:04:28.455
Part 7.

90
00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:29.653
Practice.

91
00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:37.516
Write your own complaint using the formula for a real or imagined problem (phone, app, delivery, bank).

92
00:04:38.866 --> 00:04:39.741
Part 8.

93
00:04:40.021 --> 00:04:41.066
Speak today.

94
00:04:42.316 --> 00:04:45.452
Write the complaint formula on a sticky note near your phone.

95
00:04:45.732 --> 00:04:46.649
Practise:

96
00:04:46.929 --> 00:04:48.871
Could I have the complaint number, please?

97
00:04:50.221 --> 00:04:51.757
That's the end of this lesson.

98
00:04:52.037 --> 00:04:56.687
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

99
00:04:56.967 --> 00:05:03.090
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

